From: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] software-manager: don't log the MuxOutputs probe terminator

The BIOS, CPLD and EEPROM managers all discover how many mux outputs a
configuration declares by walking Foo.MuxOutputs0, MuxOutputs1, ... until
one is missing:

    for (size_t i = 0; true; i++) { ... if (!name || !polarity) break; }

Both properties are fetched with dbusGetRequiredProperty(), which logs an
error whenever the Get fails. The interface that ends the loop always
fails, so every board with a MuxOutputs config emits two errors per scan
naming an interface that was never supposed to exist:

    Missing property Name on path .../HostSPIFlash, interface ...MuxOutputs1
    Missing property Polarity on path .../HostSPIFlash, interface ...MuxOutputs1

A correctly configured single-mux board therefore looks misconfigured.

Add dbusGetOptionalProperty() for the case where absence is an expected
answer, express dbusGetRequiredProperty() in terms of it so the logging
behaviour of every other caller is untouched, and use the optional form
for the three probe loops.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/bios/bios_software_manager.cpp b/bios/bios_software_manager.cpp
index c441284c..c9cb4010 100644
--- a/bios/bios_software_manager.cpp
+++ b/bios/bios_software_manager.cpp
@@ -66,12 +66,14 @@ sdbusplus::async::task<bool> BIOSSoftwareManager::initDevice(
     {
         const std::string iface = configIfaceMux + std::to_string(i);
 
+        // The absent interface is how this loop terminates, so it must not be
+        // reported as a missing property.
         std::optional<std::string> name =
-            co_await dbusGetRequiredProperty<std::string>(ctx, service, path,
+            co_await dbusGetOptionalProperty<std::string>(ctx, service, path,
                                                           iface, "Name");
 
         std::optional<std::string> polarity =
-            co_await dbusGetRequiredProperty<std::string>(ctx, service, path,
+            co_await dbusGetOptionalProperty<std::string>(ctx, service, path,
                                                           iface, "Polarity");
 
         if (!name.has_value() || !polarity.has_value())
diff --git a/common/include/dbus_helper.hpp b/common/include/dbus_helper.hpp
index e2e620ad..e4f1c5dd 100644
--- a/common/include/dbus_helper.hpp
+++ b/common/include/dbus_helper.hpp
@@ -8,8 +8,12 @@
 
 PHOSPHOR_LOG2_USING;
 
+// Fetch a property without complaining when it is absent. Use this when a
+// missing property is an expected outcome rather than a fault -- most notably
+// when probing an open-ended series of interfaces (Foo0, Foo1, ...) where the
+// first absent one is simply how the caller learns it has reached the end.
 template <typename T>
-sdbusplus::async::task<std::optional<T>> dbusGetRequiredProperty(
+sdbusplus::async::task<std::optional<T>> dbusGetOptionalProperty(
     sdbusplus::async::context& ctx, const std::string& service,
     const std::string& path, const std::string& intf,
     const std::string& property)
@@ -27,6 +31,21 @@ sdbusplus::async::task<std::optional<T>> dbusGetRequiredProperty(
         opt = std::get<T>(result);
     }
     catch (std::exception& e)
+    {
+        opt = std::nullopt;
+    }
+    co_return opt;
+}
+
+template <typename T>
+sdbusplus::async::task<std::optional<T>> dbusGetRequiredProperty(
+    sdbusplus::async::context& ctx, const std::string& service,
+    const std::string& path, const std::string& intf,
+    const std::string& property)
+{
+    std::optional<T> opt = co_await dbusGetOptionalProperty<T>(
+        ctx, service, path, intf, property);
+    if (!opt.has_value())
     {
         error("Missing property {PROPERTY} on path {PATH}, interface {INTF}",
               "PROPERTY", property, "PATH", path, "INTF", intf);
